**Rule (Scope ownership and completion snapshot)** · `rule:nrz:tiles-streams-graph-drain`

A scope records its graph owner, nonwrapping notification generation, roots, fixed admitted topology boundary and owned expectation/dependency closure. Before publishing the scope, reserve its membership/visited storage and pending notification records. Traverse that closure in bounded recorded edge order with idempotent generation marks. Partial notification closes only owned expectations; a shared external producer remains an explicit dependency wait and cannot be sealed on another consumer's behalf. The same resumable atomic-step rule as (`rule:nrz:tiles-streams-graph-transactions`) applies. There are no refinement children in this subset; future child support must reserve inherited scope membership before activation. Input newly admitted during draining belongs to a new graph owner. The old owner has no incremental activation and no spare edges; no cross-owner topology insertion or incremental acyclicity/readiness build is admitted. The new owner pays its complete private admission beside all old live owners and receives its own scopes. For completion inspection the caller supplies a bounded set of admitted graph owners for this heap, including any pending-only owners in that set, and serializes admissions with inspection of that set and the reconciled heap residence snapshot. Inspect each owner's completion predicate in that same snapshot; the heap accounts numerical residence and does not enumerate graph metadata. The completion result names that supplied owner set; the library cannot detect an omitted owner and never reports global completion on its own. The owner-set storage/iteration is inventoried under graph scope/observer bytes and graph record Work; no uncharged global registry is assumed. Completion for that supplied set requires every enumerated owner complete and the heap predicate empty; a new owner with only pending graph work can block completion even before it owns numerical payload (`def:nrz:tiles-streams-flush-scope`), (`rule:nrz:tiles-streams-flush-partial`).

Scope completion requires its applications and notification/control work terminal, its use edges released and its delivery obligations acknowledged. A partial completion reports surviving outside/shared occupations. Full completion additionally observes, in one serialized admission/residence snapshot, no active or waiting graph work, outstanding borrower, delivery or numerical reader, and the reconciled zero-occupied predicate of (`rule:nrz:matrix-loans-residence`). Required native reclamation passes retain their existing charged traversal; do not infer a one-pass bound from acyclicity. Report vacant table capacity, graph metadata, eligible exact authority and external history separately from occupied numerical payload. Any numerical payload still retained makes full completion false. Warm authority remains only within its existing bounded owner; no new cache or lowering reuse is established by this observation (`rule:nrz:tiles-streams-flush-completion`), (`alg:nrz:matrix-loans-retirement`).

**Rule (Stopping and abandoning the graph owner)** · `rule:nrz:tiles-streams-graph-abandonment`

A typed stop preserves the graph owner and all recoverable native capabilities for inspection, legal cancellation or resumed control work within the original allowance. Dropping the owner is abandonment, never successful flush. It cancels only detached native owners actually held by the graph through their prepaid existing cancellation paths, releases only graph-owned retention edges and destroys its reserved native tables with prepaid cleanup. It neither reclaims an outstanding host loan nor consumes an independently retained delivery reader. Those owners retain their native return/release routes and continue to appear in heap residence after the graph goes away. Separately retained scope/outcome witnesses must report abandonment rather than a completion snapshot; their bounded status/evidence storage is part of the delivery/history inventory and cannot hold a strong cycle back to the whole graph. No destructor performs fallible export, invokes a numerical kernel, traverses an unbounded history or obtains a fresh ledger. Failed required evidence delivery remains a recorded unfinished obligation, not a reason to claim empty completion (`rule:nrz:matrix-loans-cleanup-tariffs`), (`rule:nrz:tiles-streams-release`), (`rule:nrz:tiles-streams-graph-drain`). The concrete witness layout and its accounting remain subject to (`open:nrz:tiles-streams-graph-admission-gates`).

