**Requirement (Host sampling implementation evidence)** · `req:nrz:host-sampling-acceptance`

Demonstrate a host-supplied prepared operation with independently known Work, useful estimates, both throughput units and an `N`-item extrapolation. Include zero-exact-Work native evaluation and a charged operation, comparing every iteration receipt with the operation's own accounting without changing existing pins. Sample the same prepared problem twice and compare retained graph/plan/input state and live-resource inventory before and after; test failure, reset and output disposal as well as success. Show no default file/console output or process-global change, and run alongside an unrelated Criterion benchmark and a second sampler with separate seeds. Tracing enabled and disabled preserve results and Work while their timing configurations remain distinguishable.

Check the port against an independent computation on fixed sample rows: hand-derived mean, variance, scaled MAD, through-origin slope, Tukey fences and interpolated percentiles; exhaustively enumerate resample index tuples for a small dataset to verify both univariate and paired bootstrap distributions, confidence endpoints and standard errors. The oracle must not call the extracted helpers. Use explicit index sequences to distinguish statistical equivalence from RNG sequence changes, and separately pin the seeded generator/index stream. Add equal-valued data, outliers, nonfinite/zero values, invalid counts/confidence, arithmetic/allocation boundaries and reciprocal/batch overflow controls. Fixed-data analysis tests are deterministic; real-clock evidence reports observed estimates without requiring a particular timing or nominal coverage on one run.

Use a controllable clock/adapter to exhaust the budget in every phase, including warm-up, a single slow operation, reset, receipt collection, bootstrap, sorting and cleanup. Verify no new iteration is admitted after the deadline, no unfinished schedule receives a full estimate, finite memory/count caps hold, and return-time overshoot includes residual unchecked execution plus the entire mandatory finalization tail. Include a composed clock fixture with `D = 100 ms`: an operation admitted at `99 ms` runs for `8 ms`, receipt preservation then takes `3 ms` and disposal takes `8 ms`. With zero clock advance for other tail work, return is at `118 ms`, the residual after `D` is `7 ms`, and `C` covers at least the sequential `11 ms` tail; an `8 ms` maximum-component bound fails this case. Add nonzero report/cleanup costs and injected scheduling delay, verifying their additive contribution and that finalization may continue after expiry without admitting another iteration. Exercise an operation that cannot supply a cooperative bound as unsupported; hard process termination is a host responsibility. Complete workspace formatting, clippy, documentation, tests, docgen and host lint gates, with the attributed source subject to the same safety and label rules as other owned code.

**Open Question (Implementation and broader sampling capability)** · `open:nrz:host-sampling-follow-through`

The selected extraction, public operation/reset/Work adapters, bounded analysis, source notices and estimator revisions must satisfy (`req:nrz:host-sampling-acceptance`); their contribution to LC measurement standing is recorded in (`claim:nrz:lc-closing-cost-accounting`), (`claim:nrz:lc-closing-scale-measurement`). Review source subsets against an independent statistical oracle and maintain an explicit revision for changed estimator or index-selection semantics. Flat/automatic sampling, asynchronous operations, shared mutable workloads, mixed-population joint intervals, future-batch prediction intervals, parallel-batch models, portable report serialization and hard-deadline process isolation remain separate capabilities. Possible upstream public APIs and source upgrades are maintenance options, not prerequisites or fulfilled commitments.

**Definition (Phase span vocabulary)** · `def:nrz:tiles-streams-spans`

The pipeline root is `nrz.pipeline`. Its fixed phase names are `nrz.prepare`, `nrz.loan`, `nrz.handback`, `nrz.lower`, `nrz.prelude`, `nrz.walk`, `nrz.kernel`, `nrz.barrier`, `nrz.lookup`, `nrz.proof`, `nrz.replay`, `nrz.refine`, `nrz.publish`, `nrz.flush`, `nrz.deliver` and `nrz.retire`. `nrz.work.phase` marks finer existing charged helper boundaries with rule and operation fields; it is not emitted by each arithmetic charge. Every span identifies family, revision, owner, graph/application and attempt when applicable, plus parent/causal identity, claim scope, active ledger incarnation and Work at each entered interval boundary under (`def:nrz:tiles-streams-ledger-intervals`). Outcome and refusal/stop reason are recorded on exit, including failed attempts. Host fill, dependency wait and consumer wait use `nrz.wait` with a reason and monotonic duration; they declare no engine ledger when they perform no engine work. Native phases still snapshot any active exact ledger so a claimed zero can be checked.

**Definition (Construction, decision and cache events)** · `def:nrz:tiles-streams-events`

Use fixed events `nrz.construct` with object kind, action and count for descriptors, exact nodes, evidence edges, certificates, tile/mask versions, kernel applications and lowered lambdas; actions distinguish attempted, completed, retained, reused, rolled back and retired. `nrz.cas.call` counts actual CAS invocations. `nrz.pi` distinguishes full validation, authenticated citation, numerical import and prelude evaluation. `nrz.cache` reports kind, tier, probe/hit/miss/refusal/eviction, key/proof identity, entries visited, comparison extent and charged receipt reference. `nrz.replay.result` distinguishes local and portable replay. `nrz.decision` joins attempted/completed/retained/undecided/refused outcomes, original question, authority, input closure, attempt and selected continuation. The same attempt identity links cache preparation, lookup, origin checking, cut/witness checking, refinement and publication. Retained counts cannot replace attempted construction counts or conceal rolled-back exact work.

**Definition (Native work, residence and ledger events)** · `def:nrz:tiles-streams-native-events`

`nrz.mask` reports operation, words/cells visited, population and role; `nrz.layout` reports checked mapping, sorting, gather/scatter and native version-validation work. `nrz.memory` reports allocation owner, resource dimension, requested/actual capacity, bytes, allocation/deep-copy/release action and retained references. `nrz.readiness` records edge release, leaf activation and dependency/resource waits; `nrz.flush.state` records notification, scoped drain and completion with occupied heap and retained cache quantities. `nrz.claim` associates original relation, exact index/physical scope, ordered quantifiers, revisions and returned claim with the relevant span. `nrz.work.transfer` links child/private-ledger observations to an existing parent reconciliation, without debiting it again. `nrz.observer.loss` marks missing events, overflow or incomplete snapshots; absence of observed events after such a loss cannot support a zero-work claim. No event exports heap readings as exact cache keys.

**Definition (Ledger incarnations and entered interval forests)** · `def:nrz:tiles-streams-ledger-intervals`

Each ledger incarnation has a stable owner-qualified identity and nonwrapping generation for its complete observed lifetime. Distinct private, cloned or replacement ledgers have distinct identities even if their snapshots or storage addresses coincide. A span's entered interval records entry and exit snapshots on one such ledger. Project the active entered stack onto that ledger: each interval's parent is the nearest enclosing active interval on the same ledger, across intervening spans on other ledgers or no ledger; absent such an interval, it is a forest root. Causal span parentage alone does not define this relation. Instrumentation closes or splits entered intervals at suspension and ownership-transfer boundaries so intervals on one ledger are nested or disjoint. Resume opens a new interval with its current projected parent and the same causal span identity. A suspended span contributes the sum of its closed entered intervals, never a single first-entry-to-final-exit delta that includes work while it was suspended.

**Rule (Exclusive attribution subtracts same-ledger children)** · `rule:nrz:tiles-streams-attribution`

For each closed interval of (`def:nrz:tiles-streams-ledger-intervals`), inclusive Work is its exit snapshot minus its entry snapshot. Its exclusive Work subtracts only the disjoint inclusive intervals of its immediate children in that ledger's projected interval forest. Sum these exclusive deltas across a span's closed intervals for the span's exclusive receipt; descendants below an immediate child are already included in that child's subtraction. Sum exclusive classified phases and the explicit unclassified remainder to each observed ledger root delta; never clamp a negative result or hide a missing exit. One ledger has one sequential mutation owner; independent concurrent work uses distinct ledger incarnations, so unrelated elapsed overlap is not subtracted. Different-ledger Work remains separate. `nrz.work.transfer` links it to an existing parent reconciliation as a separate accounting relation, counting that debit once without making the foreign-ledger interval a subtractable child or debiting either ledger again. Failed attempts retain their spent delta; rejected charges add no invented consumption. Private or discarded ledgers must be observed before destruction and cannot disappear behind a zero caller delta.

**Rule (Observer limits cannot change arithmetic)** · `rule:nrz:tiles-streams-observer-bounds`

The layer reserves bounded active-span storage and aggregates finite vocabulary counters by declared family/owner scope, streaming detailed evidence to an explicitly bounded external sink when requested. It reports its own memory/time and completeness. Retaining every historical tile or attempt in an unbounded in-memory trace is incompatible with a bounded-residence claim. Lost observations mark that claim incomplete; subscriber failure cannot turn a successful arithmetic operation into a new mathematical refusal or change a Work limit. Tests can reject incomplete evidence in their harness. A user-visible unclassified remainder is legitimate until the coverage manifest explains it; zero prohibited kernel work requires complete coverage, not merely an empty event collection.

**Observation (Existing Work trace is a test observer)** · `obs:nrz:tiles-streams-work-trace-source`

Work-trace migration and its measured scope are recorded in (`claim:nrz:lc-closing-cost-accounting`). The test observer in `crates/cas/src/testing/work_trace.rs` is an attribution fixture; neither a fixture's complete receipts nor a zero returned caller delta establishes complete coverage of another LC route. Production boundaries and subscriber subtraction must satisfy (`req:nrz:tiles-streams-work-trace-layer`), (`req:nrz:tiles-streams-accounting-coverage`).

**Requirement (Work trace shares the subscriber layer)** · `req:nrz:tiles-streams-work-trace-layer`

The test observer must use the same boundary spans and subscriber subtraction as production observation, with no separate thread-local attribution mechanism or charge-path `record` hook. Implementation standing and LC coverage belong to (`claim:nrz:lc-closing-cost-accounting`). Existing rule/phase/location buckets are a test layer's rendering of those spans, with finer `nrz.work.phase` boundaries where the old fixture needs operation attribution. `measured` installs a scoped subscriber, runs the ordinary operation and collects the layer's completed receipts; it must retain refused attempts and detect incomplete observation. `Budget::work` remains solely deterministic limit checking and consumption, with no attribution search, allocation or subscriber error path. Preserve the complete fixture totals, their named attribution scopes and every existing literal Work pin; any migration of observation machinery requires equivalence evidence before retiring its predecessor.

**Requirement (Route coverage and exclusive receipts)** · `req:nrz:tiles-streams-accounting-coverage`

Each claimed route supplies a coverage manifest for public entry points and traversed helpers, caller/private/discarded ledgers, immutable-budget checks, charged operations and native unmetered work. Include context construction, bindings checker private budgets, binding validation, matrix symbol import, scalar enclosure arithmetic, heap and layout operations and transient descriptor construction named in (`req:nrz:lc-grid-accounting-coverage`). Place boundary spans at the actual preparation, handback, barrier lookup/origin/cut, refinement, publication, flush and replay sites. The subscriber's same-ledger exclusive receipts plus remainder must reconcile with each ledger, including refusal. Constructor/clone/allocation events cover activity that creates no net retained graph growth. These fulfill (`req:nrz:lc-grid-phase-receipts`) without moving attribution into arithmetic.

**Requirement (Scoped claims and joined attempt evidence)** · `req:nrz:tiles-streams-accounting-claims`

Use `nrz.claim` and stable application/attempt fields to distinguish whole-domain cover preparation, a fresh numerical answer, a selected exact decision and portable replay, even when they cite one lemma. Join every decision attempt's preparation, hit/miss, origin proof, cut/witness, refinement and selected publication with actual source/map/companion versions and original question. Preserve failed and undecided attempts, spent resources and last valid enclosure. Mutation controls change a source, map, unchanged-center companion and equal-valued foreign source and must invalidate or correctly revalidate the affected claim. This fulfills (`req:nrz:lc-grid-construction-events`), (`req:nrz:lc-grid-claim-scopes`) and (`req:nrz:lc-grid-decision-attempts`); a reused exact theorem never becomes evidence that a fresh answer was computed.

**Requirement (Reproducible fixtures and measurement scope)** · `req:nrz:tiles-streams-accounting-fixtures`

Publish small fixtures at multiple populations with exact input generation, complete constant/pi certificate content and revisions, source/arithmetic versions, snapshot boundaries, claim scopes and per-cell plus per-tile Work vectors under (`req:nrz:lc-grid-accounting-fixtures`). Include cold preparation, repeated retained preparation, changed keys, eviction, owner/generation changes, fresh attachments and post-flush imports. Each literal cold/warm fixture fixes initial index contents and order, retained proof choices and complete proof keys, owner/generation relationships, next admission counters, retained/reserved usage, prior cumulative usage and relevant admission/publication/rollback/eviction history under (`def:nrz:reuse-replay-state`), (`rule:nrz:tiles-streams-admission-order`). Record the selected proof and actual probe sequence; equal-state replay is distinct from comparing cold and warm states. Measure disabled tracing overhead in the same pinned environment and report it separately from enabled subscriber time/storage. The historical throwaway LC baseline lacks sufficient generator/certificate data for exact Work reproduction; preserve its reported values and identify replacement fixtures explicitly. Independent timing runs supplement the deterministic receipts, never supply their missing scope.

**Requirement (Projected attribution and lifecycle evidence)** · `req:nrz:tiles-streams-observer-evidence`

Exercise nested spans A on ledger L, B on ledger M and C on ledger L, with B between A and C in the tracing tree. With A's inclusive L delta ten and C's delta five, C is A's immediate projected child: A's exclusive L delta is five and their classified L sum is ten, while M reconciles separately. Repeat with a ledgerless wrapper in B's place. Include deeper projected descendants, multiple disjoint children and nonzero unclassified remainder. Suspend and resume a span while another span spends on the same ledger; the suspended span's receipt must sum only its closed entered intervals and must not absorb work in the gap. Combine these controls with failed attempts after a charged prefix, rejected charges, private/cloned ledger identities, destruction/recreation, and an explicit child-to-parent Work transfer. Reconcile each ledger's classified receipts and remainder independently before reconciling transfers; count the parent debit once and preserve the named attribution scopes and existing Work pins of (`req:nrz:tiles-streams-work-trace-layer`). Missing boundaries, identity ambiguity or observer loss make the evidence incomplete under (`rule:nrz:tiles-streams-observer-bounds`).

