Exercise empty, partial, sparse and full masks; padding; multi-component companions; every mask operation; demand intersections and reductions with missing operands; mask-only and compacted branches; several tiles per barrier and a barrier using part of one tile. Independent expected original-index mappings and branch/quantifier results must agree after movement. Foreign/stale/double handback must leave the rightful live loan unchanged; outstanding borrowers, changed masks/companions and protected earlier versions must prevent unsafe reads or reclamation. Exercise an authenticated genuine loan with initialized cells whose payload fails validation, and a separate fallible-publication refusal: each error must return a repairable/cancellable loan without publication. Demonstrate repair and successful handback, and failed handback followed by cancellation and full flush, with explicit ownership, reservation and absence transitions. Check walk cost counters under fan-out, release, invalidation and capacity stalls, including progress of unrelated leaves and bounded retries. Include a constant-size invalidated closure containing the only ready leaf in a large allocated bitmap: clearing it must account for every summary level even with few occupied slots. Report C, V, bitmap allocation/initialization words, traversed closure nodes/edges, changed ready bits, summary updates and mask-check work separately under (`rule:nrz:tiles-streams-walk-release`). Full flush must report zero occupied heap only after required delivery and readers release; partial flush must preserve outside consumers. Repeat at fixed capacity over increasing duration with graph, cache, provenance, observer and external-history sizes separately reported.

